{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/444936-siskur-dah-on-rescue-missions","id":444936,"title":"Siskur-Dah on Rescue Missions...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-16T15:00:54-07:00","id":444936,"title":"Siskur-Dah on Rescue Missions...","content":"Lets say someone close to the pack or a member of the pack gets captured by something bad.<br /> <br /> Is it in theme to declare that person or pack member the focus of the hunt? The hunts purpose being not to kill them, but obtain them. Would this apply to things like the Rahu's Bloody Handed Hunter Gift?<br /> <br /> Most what I'm asking is, what can and can't be the target of a hunt and for what purpose can sacred hunts be called? Are there any restrictions, limitations or clauses?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T15:08:37-07:00","id":444960,"title":"","content":"That's a very good question. <br /> <br /> What about inanimate objects? Can you declare the hunt on a McGuffin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T15:22:07-07:00","id":444977,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;On this day, we shall observe the sacred rite of <b>SISKUR-DAH!</b>&quot;<br /> &quot;Now... <i>get the ball! Get the ball! Who's a good boy??! Get the ball!</i>&quot;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T16:28:32-07:00","id":445061,"title":"","content":"You don't have to know the targets name, so you could just issue a hunt for, 'Whoever kidnapped our packmate.' With your enhanced senses you'd likely be able to have a general idea of who did it, providing you did some legwork before jumping to a sacred hunt rite before you checked your e-mail and found they had just gone out of town.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-16-2015, 07:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T17:07:25-07:00","id":445089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/444936-siskur-dah-on-rescue-missions?p=445061#post445061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't have to know the targets name, so you could just issue a hunt for, 'Whoever kidnapped our packmate.' With your enhanced senses you'd likely be able to have a general idea of who did it, providing you did some legwork before jumping to a sacred hunt rite before you checked your e-mail and found they had just gone out of town.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. I'm more thinking of valid hunt targets and the nature of the hunt.<br /> <br /> It's been said and alluded to many times before that the hunt isn't just about killing things. It's about hunting, and that can be just about anything. <br /> <br /> So what's the scope of the Siskur-Dah? It's important to define for many reasons in consistent theme and storytelling.<br /> <br /> In my example I'my wondering if you can rescue someone with it with the president your rescuing being the target of the hunt rather than targeting the kidnappers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T17:17:28-07:00","id":445093,"title":"","content":"It certainly isn't just about killing, you can use it to get gifts, for instance. Nothing says the sacred hunt has to be about killing. So you could use it to rescue someone, or to get information from someone, I think.<br /> <br /> But the rite is also supposed to be a sacred, spiritual thing for werewolves, and not something taken lightly. So for example if you were after the kidnappers, then decided to switch it to the president so you could take advantage of some gifts in a certain way might be like how a religious person would feel taking a shortcut in their prayers, or something.<br /> <br /> Offhand I wouldn't think an inanimate object would apply.<br /> <br /> Of course I'm not a writer or anything and am basing this off what's in the book, and my opinions about that sort of thing don't seem popular.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-16-2015, 08:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T17:51:59-07:00","id":445116,"title":"","content":"Because stuff like Bloody Handed Hunter work on anything stopping you from getting to your Prey, not on the prey themselves.<br /> <br /> The Cahalith can find the prey's rough physical location, or can make them Open...<br /> ... which is synergistic with the Itheur's ability to better travel the Shadow.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Elodeth is boosting their Allies' ability to find their kidnapped packmate, and the Rahu and Irraka are running a bloody line right to their doorstep.<br /> <br /> It doesn't really matter if the kidnappers get away; you achieved your goal.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T09:41:20-07:00","id":446057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/444936-siskur-dah-on-rescue-missions?p=445116#post445116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because stuff like Bloody Handed Hunter work on anything stopping you from getting to your Prey, not on the prey themselves.<br /> <br /> The Cahalith can find the prey's rough physical location, or can make them Open...<br /> ... which is synergistic with the Itheur's ability to better travel the Shadow.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Elodeth is boosting their Allies' ability to find their kidnapped packmate, and the Rahu and Irraka are running a bloody line right to their doorstep.<br /> <br /> It doesn't really matter if the kidnappers get away; you achieved your goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. <br /> <br /> So is the general consensus that 'hunt' is very subjective, and more liken to a goal or objective rather than traditional conceptions of hunting?<br /> <br /> Creative hunters and curious minds want to know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T10:41:34-07:00","id":446166,"title":"","content":"Given that the main supernatural interaction in the werewolf game is with spirits, who are naturally subjective and conceptual, hunting down concepts and states of being makes total sense.<br /> In your example, you are hunting for your friend's safe return, with sub-prey of their current location and exit routes.<br /> If you're going after opening the Gift of Weather, as nofather pointed out as being a good non-kill example, you're hunting down a pact, with a sub-prey of (a) weather (spirit).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T11:05:10-07:00","id":446197,"title":"","content":"Spirits of abstract concepts are still actual things you can hunt though. You're heading into Fae territory with those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T13:37:51-07:00","id":446488,"title":"","content":"I fully intend in my upcoming Detroit game to have an Iron Master declare Siskur-Dah on the city zoning laws.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T13:47:22-07:00","id":446495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/444936-siskur-dah-on-rescue-missions?p=446488#post446488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fully intend in my upcoming Detroit game to have an Iron Master declare Siskur-Dah on the city zoning laws.</div> </div> </div> </div>... How do you imagine that working? <br /> <br /> I don't mean to come across as dubious that it CAN work. I just have trouble envisioning how Iron Masters conduct hunts on human organizations and how zoning laws fits into this... <br /> <br /> So if you've imagine something playing out, I'd love to hear it to help give myself better understanding as to how something like that can be implemented!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T16:03:06-07:00","id":446639,"title":"","content":"Have you seen the new Gifts?!? I imagine heated exchanges during city council meetings with Flaring Renown, Primal Allure in darkened offices, last minute re-drafting of legislation under threat of Hard Leverage, using Unity to bolster an alderman packmate during an important argument, using Needle to search out obscure bylaws or dirt on the mayor, Sounds of the City to cut opponents off from their allies and resource, and Garble to curse the head of the opposition when he needs to make calls to thwart the pack's efforts. Then, in the end, victory! The law is amended to allow urban gardening and the keeping of animals. The source of fresh meat for the pack is secured! Let us feast!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T16:55:36-07:00","id":446710,"title":"","content":"That's awesome and I look forward to hearing about how it went down when someone actually attempts that.<br /> Quick note on Needle, since your story will flow better if everyone is on the same page mechanically: its for putting things into haystacks, not taking them out. You'd use it when you know the loophole to make sure your opponent doesn't. Somehow you find out about the bit of precedence that will wreck their case at the critical moment when they didn't know about it, then you use Needle and it slips their minds and they lose the documentation about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T19:57:51-07:00","id":446961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/444936-siskur-dah-on-rescue-missions?p=446639#post446639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you seen the new Gifts?!? I imagine heated exchanges during city council meetings with Flaring Renown, Primal Allure in darkened offices, last minute re-drafting of legislation under threat of Hard Leverage, using Unity to bolster an alderman packmate during an important argument, using Needle to search out obscure bylaws or dirt on the mayor, Sounds of the City to cut opponents off from their allies and resource, and Garble to curse the head of the opposition when he needs to make calls to thwart the pack's efforts. Then, in the end, victory! The law is amended to allow urban gardening and the keeping of animals. The source of fresh meat for the pack is secured! Let us feast!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How would Flaring Renown benefit the werewolf during council meetings? It was my understanding that Flaring Renown is ineffective against normal humans. The text specifically states, &quot; . . .an Uratha can intensify her spirit brands by spending a point of Essence, letting her Renown speak for itself. This even makes the brands faintly visible in the physical world. Uratha, spirits, Wolf-Blooded, and others attuned to the spirit world intuitively understand not only what Renown the brands reflect but the deeds she accomplished to get them.&quot;<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, I definitely like your sacred hunt idea to change the zoning laws in Detroit. It would be most interesting, however, if the opponents of the new law are other uratha, vampires or mages with significant supernatural resources and hard leverage of their own. No pack should ever become to cocky, particularly in the WOD. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T20:26:45-07:00","id":446987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/444936-siskur-dah-on-rescue-missions?p=446961#post446961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would Flaring Renown benefit the werewolf during council meetings? It was my understanding that Flaring Renown is ineffective against normal humans. The text specifically states, &quot; . . .an Uratha can intensify her spirit brands by spending a point of Essence, letting her Renown speak for itself. This even makes the brands faintly visible in the physical world. Uratha, spirits, Wolf-Blooded, and others attuned to the spirit world intuitively understand not only what Renown the brands reflect but the deeds she accomplished to get them.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't notice that. Still getting used to the new rules. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nevertheless, I definitely like your sacred hunt idea to change the zoning laws in Detroit. It would be most interesting, however, if the opponents of the new law are other uratha, vampires or mages with significant supernatural resources and hard leverage of their own. No pack should ever become to cocky, particularly in the WOD. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>Can't imagine there wouldn't be some sort of colorful Claimed in there somewhere. Also, I could see the spirit of the city being irked by their interference if they didn't seek permission first. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T20:41:12-07:00","id":447019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/444936-siskur-dah-on-rescue-missions?p=446639#post446639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you seen the new Gifts?!? I imagine heated exchanges during city council meetings with Flaring Renown, Primal Allure in darkened offices, last minute re-drafting of legislation under threat of Hard Leverage, using Unity to bolster an alderman packmate during an important argument, using Needle to search out obscure bylaws or dirt on the mayor, Sounds of the City to cut opponents off from their allies and resource, and Garble to curse the head of the opposition when he needs to make calls to thwart the pack's efforts. Then, in the end, victory! The law is amended to allow urban gardening and the keeping of animals. The source of fresh meat for the pack is secured! Let us feast!</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, thank you. I can see what angle you're going at with this. ^.^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T20:45:15-07:00","id":447028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/444936-siskur-dah-on-rescue-missions?p=446987#post446987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Didn't notice that. Still getting used to the new rules. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, who's to say one of the People can't hold public office? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T21:52:50-07:00","id":447129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/444936-siskur-dah-on-rescue-missions?p=446987#post446987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Didn't notice that. Still getting used to the new rules. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I was just re-reading the various Renown Conditions referenced in the flaring section and their indicated sources. The text is, at best, vague concerning whether normal humans would be subject to an uratha's flaring of their renown. I'm now actually more confused than before as to whether Flaring Renown only affects spirit-y beings, everyone including normal humans, or anyone who actually sees the Renown brands regardless of their spiritual or supernatural status, as the Renown text indicates that when flared, the brands are in fact &quot;faintly visible in the material world.&quot; (p. 99).<br /> <br /> An answer or FAQ by anyone from the WtF 2e development team would certainly be most helpful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alternatively, who's to say one of the People can't hold public office? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>I can certainly see a werewolf holding office, particularly an Iron Master. In fact, eberg indicated that in his scenario, a werewolf could use his gifts to bolster an alderman packmate.<br /> <br /> Since this is the WOD, and the population of supernatural beings is apparently huge and growing, it wouldn't surprise me if there are no normal humans in any major government positions, or if so, they are just puppets of more powerful creatures, both utterly evil and benign.<br /> <br /> Could you imagine being some poor schlub of a community activist testifying before a local zoning subcommittee comprising an Iron Master Uratha, Invictus Vampire and Mastigos Mage, in a building located on a spiritual locus within a haunted hearing room? If you don't have some supernatural mojo, it sometimes barely pays to wake-up in the morning in the WOD. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can't imagine there wouldn't be some sort of colorful Claimed in there somewhere. Also, I could see the spirit of the city being irked by their interference if they didn't seek permission first. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>Given both the long and storied history of Detroit and its current state of disrepair and despair, its spirit ecology would be most interesting. I can easily imagine that a decaying spirit of the city fighting for supremacy with a bankruptcy spirit of false hope, a city manager spirit of outside dominance and loss of control, spirits of great innovation and stultifying stagnation, and hosts of colorful union spirits ranging from greed and failure to industriousness and solidarity. Or maybe, WOD Detroit's problems are actually the result of a barren spiritscape caused by the long deprivations of a powerful Azulu, or worse, an<i> idigam</i> . . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 03-18-2015, 12:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T04:16:29-07:00","id":447472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/444936-siskur-dah-on-rescue-missions?p=446961#post446961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would Flaring Renown benefit the werewolf during council meetings? It was my understanding that Flaring Renown is ineffective against normal humans. The text specifically states, &quot; . . .an Uratha can intensify her spirit brands by spending a point of Essence, letting her Renown speak for itself. This even makes the brands faintly visible in the physical world. Uratha, spirits, Wolf-Blooded, and others attuned to the spirit world intuitively understand not only what Renown the brands reflect but the deeds she accomplished to get them.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, I'm not on the development team like you asked for in having someone clarify this, but I've got something of an explaanation.<br /> When you flare your Renown, people and things attuned to the spirit world can see your brands and understand what's going on, but even those who don't know what's happening get drawn in by the power of the action. You flare up your Honor Renown and people feel pulled to try taking advantage of you. When they do, your next success at Empathy, Politics, or Socialize is assured and proobably amazing. At Honor 5, you don't even need to get any successes on the roll for it to be an Exceptional Success. The bonus to your roll has nothing to do with the people around you knowing what just happened.<br /> <br /> Now, you could take this a second, and perhaps easier way. Assuming the courtroom scenario was going to just have one such roll in it, you can gather your pack/legal team just before the hearing, flare up and have a pack mate take the pot shot. Your mantle and success are secured and all your opponent ever has to know is you are on your game today. This method is alluded to somewhere in one of the sections on flaring when it talks about how pack mates questioning your judgement in times like this (just after you flare, thereby setting off the trigger for many bonus successes for you) are very rarely censured for what could appear to be insolence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4563,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","user":"TerraBen","date":".  missed a word 03-18-2015, 07:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T05:08:39-07:00","id":447543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/444936-siskur-dah-on-rescue-missions?p=446710#post446710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick note on Needle, since your story will flow better if everyone is on the same page mechanically: its for putting things into haystacks, not taking them out. You'd use it when you know the loophole to make sure your opponent doesn't. Somehow you find out about the bit of precedence that will wreck their case at the critical moment when they didn't know about it, then you use Needle and it slips their minds and they lose the documentation about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mixed it up with Sift the Sands. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T05:16:28-07:00","id":447585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/444936-siskur-dah-on-rescue-missions?p=447129#post447129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given both the long and storied history of Detroit and its current state of disrepair and despair, its spirit ecology would be most interesting. I can easily imagine that a decaying spirit of the city fighting for supremacy with a bankruptcy spirit of false hope, a city manager spirit of outside dominance and loss of control, spirits of great innovation and stultifying stagnation, and hosts of colorful union spirits ranging from greed and failure to industriousness and solidarity. Or maybe, WOD Detroit's problems are actually the result of a barren spiritscape caused by the long deprivations of a powerful Azulu, or worse, an<i> idigam</i> . . .</div> </div> </div> </div>I am using the Nain Rouge as the city's spirit and it isn't really benevolent. It was originally a nature spirit of the area and one of the early Uratha made a severe misstep in dealing with it when the city was founded (see the Cadillac legend), making it adversarial to the human inhabitants. In my game, the Marche du Nain Rouge was started by a downtown pack in an attempt to appease the spirit, to facilitate the city's recovery.<br /> <br /> Also, of course there is an idigam. It coalesced during the 1967 riots. You can imagine how that's gone. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T06:25:22-07:00","id":447618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/444936-siskur-dah-on-rescue-missions?p=446639#post446639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you seen the new Gifts?!? I imagine heated exchanges during city council meetings with Flaring Renown, Primal Allure in darkened offices, last minute re-drafting of legislation under threat of Hard Leverage, using Unity to bolster an alderman packmate during an important argument, using Needle to search out obscure bylaws or dirt on the mayor, Sounds of the City to cut opponents off from their allies and resource, and Garble to curse the head of the opposition when he needs to make calls to thwart the pack's efforts. Then, in the end, victory! The law is amended to allow urban gardening and the keeping of animals. The source of fresh meat for the pack is secured! Let us feast!</div> </div> </div> </div>Welp. You just sorta cemented my Elodoth Iron Master environmental activist.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently playing at Fabula Rasa in the Cold Equations venue; planning an Obrimos for Fallen London.<br /> I can also be found at <a href=\"http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2192-heu","name":"Heu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T07:40:35-07:00","id":447667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/444936-siskur-dah-on-rescue-missions?p=447028#post447028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively, who's to say one of the People can't hold public office? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Our Pack Alpha (Iron Master Irraka) is the Mayor of San Francisco... Talk about all sorts of messed up... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T08:18:49-07:00","id":447725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/444936-siskur-dah-on-rescue-missions?p=446639#post446639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you seen the new Gifts?!? I imagine heated exchanges during city council meetings with Flaring Renown, Primal Allure in darkened offices, last minute re-drafting of legislation under threat of Hard Leverage, using Unity to bolster an alderman packmate during an important argument, using Needle to search out obscure bylaws or dirt on the mayor, Sounds of the City to cut opponents off from their allies and resource, and Garble to curse the head of the opposition when he needs to make calls to thwart the pack's efforts. Then, in the end, victory! The law is amended to allow urban gardening and the keeping of animals. The source of fresh meat for the pack is secured! Let us feast!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm expecting that, over time, people will become more familiar with the options amongst the new Facets and just what they can achieve with them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T08:47:41-07:00","id":447738,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of the Hunt being metaphorical as much as it is physical. You can hunt down goals and objectives without them being physically represented. You can Hunt a new job--imagine your Rahu packmate using his Facets to demolish your competition for that job you want, or walking in on your interview and totally destroying, socially speaking, any of your would-be employer's concerns and reservations.<br /> <br /> Watch an episode of <i>House of Lies</i> and tell me the way Marty Kaan and his team approach their consulting meetings <i>isn't</i> absolutely reminiscent to the Hunt: they Hunt that big fucking shower of money that comes with making a fat company pay them millions for that motherload of prey: the <i>Afterwork</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3855,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","user":"gebbethine","date":". 03-18-2015, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T09:27:17-07:00","id":447800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/444936-siskur-dah-on-rescue-missions?p=447028#post447028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively, who's to say one of the People can't hold public office? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Philidelphia has a Storm Lord as mayor in mine. He's planning on retiring from that position though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T10:01:00-07:00","id":447875,"title":"","content":"I always thought mayors and town councilpeople would make good PCs. Never did it myself but glad to see others have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T11:05:48-07:00","id":447963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/444936-siskur-dah-on-rescue-missions?p=447618#post447618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Welp. You just sorta cemented my Elodoth Iron Master environmental activist.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The problems really start to mount when your opposition from the Chamber of Commerce or unions is also an Elodoth Iron Master from a different pack (or maybe an Ivory Claw, or even a vampire or mage). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T11:07:24-07:00","id":447964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/444936-siskur-dah-on-rescue-missions?p=447725#post447725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm expecting that, over time, people will become more familiar with the options amongst the new Facets and just what they can achieve with them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Chris, could you possibly offer some guidance on our earlier discussion in the thread concerning whether Flaring Renown is effective against normal humans? Thanks.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T11:18:41-07:00","id":447972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/444936-siskur-dah-on-rescue-missions?p=447964#post447964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Chris, could you possibly offer some guidance on our earlier discussion in the thread concerning whether Flaring Renown is effective against normal humans? Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't write the section on flaring Renown or the Renown Conditions, but my understanding is that the effects of the Renown Conditions work through humans just as they would through any other character who matches the Condition's specified behaviour - for example, a human attempting to fool or take advantage of an Uratha under the Honorable Condition gains the +2 dice bonus and allows for the Uratha to meet the Resolution criteria for the Condition.<br /> <br /> Even so, you need to be careful about flaring Renown even with humans - as the rules say, 'This even makes the brands faintly visible in the physical world.' Best hope your brands aren't anywhere visible and you're covering up lots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T12:29:04-07:00","id":448032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/444936-siskur-dah-on-rescue-missions?p=447972#post447972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't write the section on flaring Renown or the Renown Conditions, but my understanding is that the effects of the Renown Conditions work through humans just as they would through any other character who matches the Condition's specified behaviour - for example, a human attempting to fool or take advantage of an Uratha under the Honorable Condition gains the +2 dice bonus and allows for the Uratha to meet the Resolution criteria for the Condition.<br /> <br /> Even so, you need to be careful about flaring Renown even with humans - as the rules say, 'This even makes the brands faintly visible in the physical world.' Best hope your brands aren't anywhere visible and you're covering up lots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hrm... <br /> <br /> So Flaring Renown isn't strictly something that's based off of a ritualistic call and response, but has more of a factor of reassuring the werewolf that their reputation is earned? <br /> <br /> Like an Irraka having privately flared their Renown and succeed say to themselves &quot;Yeah, I've still got it&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T12:50:21-07:00","id":448076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/444936-siskur-dah-on-rescue-missions?p=447972#post447972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't write the section on flaring Renown or the Renown Conditions, but my understanding is that the effects of the Renown Conditions work through humans just as they would through any other character who matches the Condition's specified behaviour - for example, a human attempting to fool or take advantage of an Uratha under the Honorable Condition gains the +2 dice bonus and allows for the Uratha to meet the Resolution criteria for the Condition.<br /> <br /> Even so, you need to be careful about flaring Renown even with humans - as the rules say, 'This even makes the brands faintly visible in the physical world.' Best hope your brands aren't anywhere visible and you're covering up lots.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks, Chris. Your continued insight as one of the authors is most helpful and welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T13:03:35-07:00","id":448122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/444936-siskur-dah-on-rescue-missions?p=448032#post448032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hrm...<br /> <br /> So Flaring Renown isn't strictly something that's based off of a ritualistic call and response, but has more of a factor of reassuring the werewolf that their reputation is earned?<br /> <br /> Like an Irraka having privately flared their Renown and succeed say to themselves &quot;Yeah, I've still got it&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a show of dominance, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T13:28:18-07:00","id":448160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/444936-siskur-dah-on-rescue-missions?p=448122#post448122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a show of dominance, yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>But can be a show of dominance that only the werewolf needs to know about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link"